      "id": 19,
      "question": "What is the difference between using OAuth2 with Password and hashing and Bearer with JWT tokens in FastAPI?",
      "answer": "OAuth2 with Password (and hashing) and Bearer with JWT tokens are both used for securing APIs, but they differ in how they handle authentication and authorization. OAuth2 with Password (and hashing) uses a password-based authentication method, while Bearer with JWT tokens uses a JSON Web Token (JWT) for authentication. OAuth2 with Password (and hashing) allows for more fine-grained permissions through scopes, while Bearer with JWT tokens are used for a more fine-grained permission system. OAuth2 with scopes is commonly used by big authentication providers like Facebook, Google, GitHub, Microsoft, Twitter, etc. to authorize third-party applications",
