      "question": "What is the difference between `Field` and `Query`, `Path`, and `Body` in the context of FastAPI?",
      "answer": "In the context of FastAPI, `Field`, `Query`, `Path`, and `Body` are used to define parameters in API operations. `Field` is used to specify the type of the parameter, while `Query`, `Path`, and `Body` are used to specify how the parameter should be interpreted from the request. `Query` and `Path` are used to interpret the parameter as a query parameter or path parameter, respectively, while `Body` is used to interpret the parameter as a request body. The `Field` parameter is also used to specify the default value of the parameter.",
